{
  "recommendation": "For your priorities—avoiding fees and maximizing the net return on $5,000—I would choose the Green Account (savings) plus the EcoCard, subject to confirming the EcoCard has no annual fee before applying.",
  "why": {
    "savings": {
      "account": "Green Account (savings)",
      "effective_apy_with_ecocard": "4.5% (4.0% base APY plus 0.5% EcoCard bonus)",
      "estimated_interest_on_5000": "$225 over one year",
      "maintenance_fee": "$0",
      "minimum_balance": "$500"
    },
    "ecocard": {
      "estimated_rewards_on_your_spending": "$12–$24 over one year on $100–$200 of monthly ordinary spending",
      "green_merchant_rewards": "Eligible eco-certified purchases may earn an additional 2.0% cash-back bonus",
      "additional_benefit": "The Green Account/EcoCard combination provides up to $20 per month in ATM-fee rebates and up to 15 free withdrawals per month",
      "annual_fee": "Not stated in the available product information, so confirm this before applying"
    },
    "estimated_total_before_any_ecocard_fee": "$237–$249, excluding any extra green-merchant rewards"
  },
  "alternative_not_preferred": {
    "combination": "Gold Account plus Gold Rewards Card",
    "savings_interest": "$276.25 at 5.525% APY on $5,000",
    "rho_bank_plus_cost": "$59.88 over one year",
    "gold_card_rewards": "$30–$60 at your expected spending level",
    "estimated_net_before_other_fees": "$246.37–$276.37",
    "concerns": [
      "The Gold Rewards Card requires Rho Bank Plus, so the subscription substantially reduces the advantage.",
      "The Gold Account documentation says a $10 monthly fee may apply below $10,000, while the Gold Rewards Card documentation says it reduces the minimum to $5,000. Because those terms conflict, I would not recommend this option without confirming that no $10 monthly fee will apply to your $5,000 balance.",
      "Your Light Blue checking account did not appear in the available product documentation, so I cannot confirm that it qualifies for any checking-linked savings boost."
    ]
  },
  "bottom_line": "Use the Green Account (savings) with the EcoCard if its annual fee is $0. If the EcoCard has an annual fee, the fee could eliminate its advantage, and I would verify the fee before opening it. I would avoid paying for Rho Bank Plus solely to obtain the Gold Rewards Card unless you confirm that the Gold Account will not charge the $10 monthly fee and you are comfortable with the subscription cost.",
  "important_caveat": "I searched for the exact Light Blue checking account but found no matching product record. I have not changed or opened any accounts."
}
